      "observed": "On the CAN BUS sheet, U30 pin 16 (CS) is labeled NET0036, and the same NET0036 label also appears on the CAN transceiver/connector path (e.g. U43 CANH side and J5/J14 pin 2). This places the MCP2515 chip-select net on the same net as a CAN bus signal/connector pin, and the two CAN connectors share corresponding CAN signal labels.",
      "expected": "The specification describes two separate isolated CAN buses (CAN0/CAN1), each with its own MCP2515 and isolated transceiver. The SPI chip-select for U30 should be a separate GPIO net, and CAN0/CAN1 CANH/CANL nets should not be merged or shared between the two buses.",
