        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (U8, U9) through an isolated CAN transceiver ... broken out on M12 circular connectors"}
      ],
      "impact": "CAN1's SPI chip-select is shorted to a CAN bus line/connector net, preventing proper SPI selection of U30 and loading/merging the CAN bus signals. This would corrupt or disable communication on the affected CAN interface and defeat the intended two-bus architecture.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic appears to merge an SPI chip-select net with a CAN bus signal net on the CAN1 interface, and the two CAN connectors share corresponding CAN signal labels, contrary to the intended two separate isolated CAN buses."
}

